+keeps the error in `error`. Acme's retries of an event we already have are
+acknowledged as duplicates, so a failed event is not retried on its own; once
+the cause is fixed (for example the payment a refund belongs to has arrived),
+an operator replays it with `POST /admin/events/:id/replay`. Every event
+carries `replayCount` and `replayedAt`, the time of its last replay.
+
+```sh
+# find failed events, then replay one by its id
+curl -s 'localhost:3000/admin/events?status=failed' -H 'x-admin-key: admin-dev-key'
+curl -s -X POST localhost:3000/admin/events/<id>/replay \
+  -H 'x-admin-key: admin-dev-key'
+```
